{
  "_why": "Known Issue 24, user ruling R3 (2026-09-23): the two families the design system picked are self-hosted. Each file below is copied unchanged from the npm package named beside it and is served from public/fonts/ at a path that never changes (a new version is a new file name). Subsetting: the packages' own latin and latin-ext unicode-range subsets, no custom cut; latin is preloaded on every page, latin-ext is fetched only by a page that uses a character in its range. Fraunces is the 'standard' file (weight and optical-size axes, the two the boards requested from Google Fonts); Source Sans 3 is the weight axis. Upright only: no page sets italic, so the browser's slanted fallback serves an <em>. tests/py/test_self_hosted_fonts.py checks every size and sha256 below.",
